Colour was one of the things we debated longest while building NanumOS. This blog is painted the same way: five colours, no more.

## Five colours and their jobs

- **Deep navy**: text and headings, the backbone of the screen
- **Coral**: buttons and highlights, where the eye should land first
- **Saffron**: rules and underlines, small joys
- **Teal**: links and sub-headings
- **Sand**: boxes on the background, quotes

## Written as code

```
:root {
  --fg:   #1D3557;  /* deep navy */
  --ac:   #E76F51;  /* coral */
  --gold: #E9C46A;  /* saffron */
  --link: #2A9D8F;  /* teal */
  --card: #F4E9D8;  /* sand */
}
```

![Navy and gold waves](media/wave.jpg)
![Navy and gold facets](media/facets.jpg)

> More colours do not make a page richer. Clear roles do.

### Try it yourself

1. Pick the one text colour you will use most
2. Add one accent that pulls the eye
3. Let the other three bridge the two

